    "narrative": "The centerpiece of today\u2019s offensive strategy is **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, who boasts an elite score of 87.22. Despite a difficult matchup against Cole, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** benefits from a strong wind-out projection and a significant BvP edge, making him a locked-in pillar for our production today. Outside of him, our highest-upside play is **Lawrence Butler** (57.49). Although he faces a left-handed pitcher, the favorable SP_xERA of 5.35 allows him to capitalize on a soft matchup, elevating his score well above the rest of our mid-tier starters. Conversely, we are tracking **Taylor Ward** (51.82) and **Gleyber Torres** (50.75) closely; both benefit from the premium leadoff spot, which provides a vital floor for our Runs and SB output, despite facing formidable arms like Gilbert and Bradley.\n\nManagement of our bench remains critical as we balance daily efficiency against our game caps. **Matt Chapman** (40.55) was the most difficult exclusion from the starting nine. While his power profile is attractive, his projected spot in the bottom third of the order against Alvarez ultimately pushed his score below the threshold required to displace **Jung Hoo Lee** or **Gavin Sheets**. We are keeping a close eye on the weather; both **Gleyber Torres** and **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** are carrying rain risk warnings. Should those contests be delayed or postponed, we will be forced to pivot to our bench depth. We continue to monitor the status of **Cal Raleigh** and **Tyler Freeman**, as their absence on the IL thins our available pinch-hitting options for late-game tactical adjustments.",
